<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 27,870,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 27,870,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors</p>
<p>Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members</p>
<p>(crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 04/02/97    03/26/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 27,870,000  28,222,000-R  25,206,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 184,382	98,648	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  35,324,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,516,775	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members</p>
<p>reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not</p>
<p>agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised from 28,321,000</p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity</p>
<p>use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   04/02/97    03/26/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,711,000   4,999,000     4,036,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,950,000   5,197,000     4,338,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,355,000   4,208,000*    4,406,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,777,000   2,931,000     2,434,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,043,000   3,933,000     3,077,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,071,000   5,036,000     5,002,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,964,000   1,918,000     1,913,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	27,870,000  28,222,000**  25,206,000</p>
<p>*Revised from 4,308,000  **Revised from 28,321,000</p>
</text>
